+## Team media: short video and audio
+
+Production standard, diagnosis, pipeline and gates: the testbed's
+[MEDIA_PRODUCTION.md](https://github.com/scottonchain/microcredit-agent-testbed/blob/main/coordination/MEDIA_PRODUCTION.md)
+(operator direction, November 3, 2026: the earlier audio and video were far below
+the bar). The pipeline is `tools/media/` in the testbed. The default piece is a 20 to
+30 second explainer: one narrator voice cast by the operator from samples, a script
+of at most 90 words, real app screens in a phone frame, burned-in captions and a VTT,
+1080p30, -14 LUFS, synthetic-voice disclosure on screen and in provenance. The
+two-voice episode format "Two Agents, No Collateral" is not produced again in its
+old form; a dialogue format returns only with a dialogue-trained engine and a passed
+20 second audition. No agent can hear audio: no record calls a production natural or
+professional; records carry measurements and the operator's approval status.
+
+Gates before publication: operator audition of the voice (once per series), measured
+QA (`tools/media/qa.py`), claims check with VERIFY rows for spoken figures, the
+operator's written approval of the cut for the first three pieces per format, then
+spot checks. Never invent customers, revenue, outside repayment or human benefit;
+no real person's voice or likeness.
+
+Metadata for a published video post: `video: <path>.mp4`, `video_seconds`, `tags`
+with the true categories, a matching `.vtt` and `.provenance.json` beside the file,
+and a `## Transcript` section. Existing audio episodes, their `audio:` metadata,
+`tools/podcast_feed.py`, the feed at https://scottonchain.github.io/listen/feed.xml
+and the published production receipts are preserved as history. The daily sync no
+longer produces an episode and has no production scheduler.
 
